uctal cells fills and distends a small duct  they appear slightly enlarged and they possess ample  eosinophilic cytoplasm and nuclei containing homogeneous chromatin  atypical columnar cells growing in a single layer and forming stubby small papillae distend a collection of glands  but distortion of the tissue makes it difficult to evaluate this focus  i acknowledge that the degree of proliferation in these areas seem slight and the nature of the cytological atypicality subtle  nevertheless  i would urge the patient and her physicians to consider an excision of this region of the left breast  examination of a larger sample would provide a more secure evaluation of the extent and the significance of the atypical ductal hyperplasia   final diagnosis by  nicole a  mihok  m d  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj notes  removed_date  received all 6 slides and report from mgh via mail  nam mi  cr  removed_date  rec d mgh path report via fax  dg removed_date  report faxed from mgh  jam removed_date  per nam  sent for opinion to mgh  dr  koerner  sent  6  slides labeled  1 1l 3l  2 1l 3l  nam dg co edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  pat indmcodes   removed_accession_id    left breast  no needle breanbx  removed_accession_id     breanbx atypical hyperp edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murjcopies to  selland donna lee m d  newton wellesley radiology newton  ma  removed_case_id   617 243  removed_case_id  skornik ronee a  m d  173 worcester st  wellesley  ma  removed_case_id   781 237  removed_case_id markers  breast disease related  presented at breast ca conf   consult case out  consult case return edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  pat indm removed_date    removed_case_id  pat 